# Build-context filter for the PARENT-context build (docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: ..` so the Dockerfile can COPY the sibling juena-core source).
#
# Docker looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` first and only falls back to a
# `.dockerignore` at the context root. The context root here is the parent
# directory, which has no `.dockerignore` -- so this file is the ONLY filter in
# effect and this repository's own `.dockerignore` is never consulted. Anything
# missing here is sent to the daemon.
#
# That parent directory holds roughly nine gigabytes across a dozen unrelated
# repositories, several of which contain real credentials in their own `.env`.
# So the rule is deny-by-default: exclude every top-level entry, re-admit only
# the two repositories this image is built from, then prune inside them.

# 1. Everything in the parent, including unrelated repositories, loose data
#    files and notebooks.
*

# 2. The two repositories the build reads, and nothing else.
!juena-chatbot
!juena-core

# 3. Prune inside them. Order matters: these follow the re-admissions above, and
#    for any given path the last matching pattern wins.

# Credentials. The application reads .env at runtime from a read-only mount
# (docker-compose.dev.yml), never from the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.streamlit/secrets.toml
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt

# Version control and virtual environments. The two .venv directories are about
# half a gigabyte each and are rebuilt inside the image by `uv sync`.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Python build, test and tool output.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.claude
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/build
**/dist
**/filesystem_dist
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# Tests. The Dockerfile copies neither repository's suite; excluding them keeps
# the context small and keeps this honest about what ships.
juena-chatbot/tests
juena-core/tests
juena-core/examples
juena-core/scripts

# Runtime state and local data. `data/` alone is the largest single directory in
# either repository -- cloned repositories, artifacts and audit logs, all of
# which are Docker volumes at runtime.
juena-chatbot/data
juena-chatbot/.sandbox
juena-chatbot/benchmarks
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.log
**/logs

# Internal development notes. Untracked on purpose and not for distribution.
juena-chatbot/DOCS
juena-core/DOCS

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
